{"family": "zoedepth", "task": "depth", "name": "ZoeDepth", "plain": "ZoeDepth from the Intelligent Systems Lab: metric depth from one image, for indoor and outdoor scenes.", "summary": "ZoeDepth (Bhat et al. 2023): metric monocular depth from a MiDaS v3.1 BEiT-L/16 core with metric-bins heads (NYU indoor, KITTI outdoor) chosen by a learned domain router (ZoeD_M12_NK).", "tier": "stable", "upstream": "https://github.com/isl-org/ZoeDepth", "upstream_commit": "d87f17b", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "ZoeDepth: Zero-shot Transfer by Combining Relative and Metric Depth", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12288", "date": "2023-02-23", "venue": "arXiv", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["cudnn_hacc"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "pad_input", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "flip", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "depth", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"kind": "metric"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["torch.compile(fullgraph=True) and torch.export are not supported: graph break in the vendored MiDaS core call and data-dependent NYU / KITTI head routing (documented xfail).", "Inputs below 5 px per side raise InputError when pad_input is on."], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: a depth or inverse-depth map. `kind` (a card field, `result.kind`) says what the numbers mean: `metric` = metres; `scale_invariant`, `affine_invariant` and `affine_invariant_inverse` are relative (unknown scale or shift, not metres). Metric models that use the focal length take `model(image, intrinsics=K)` (K `[3, 3]`, pixels of the input): `metric3d-vit-large` and `da3metric-large` need it for correct metres (`da3metric-large`: metres = output x focal / 300; without `intrinsics=` a 300 px focal length is assumed, wrong for a real camera). `unidepth-v2-vitl14`, `unik3d-vitl`, `depth-pro` and MoGe estimate the camera themselves (given `intrinsics=` replace `fx`); `zoedepth-nk` and the relative models (`da3mono-large` too) take none.", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "zoedepth-nk", "released": "0.1.1", "ref": "zoedepth-nk@1", "name": "zoedepth-nk", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "MIT", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "MIT (assumed from code)", "weights_assumed": true, "evidence": "https://github.com/isl-org/ZoeDepth/blob/d87f17b2f5fdcb174cf4fb115491f4a6c60de152/LICENSE (weights are release assets of the same repository)", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "MiDaS v3.1 BEiT-L relative-depth pre-training on 12 datasets, then metric fine-tuning on NYU Depth V2 and KITTI (ZoeDepth paper, arXiv 2302.12288)", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["weights licence not stated by the original authors; assumed to be the code licence", "data: unstated"]}, "weights": [{"name": "ZoeD_M12_NK.pt", "sha256": "5d26daa15d420eb2908f1f486a37cc84e7a91751b44ce4b4d104eb8e433f9813", "size": 1448574259, "url": "https://github.com/isl-org/ZoeDepth/releases/download/v1.0/ZoeD_M12_NK.pt", "host": "GitHub", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 8, resized or padded inside the model", "tested_max": {"size": "3000x4000", "alloc_mib": 2451, "reserved_mib": 2658}, "speed": {"standard": "994x1482", "inputs": [{"input": "518x770", "scene": "synthetic", "standard": false, "modes": {"original16": {"ms": 249.9, "peak_alloc_mb": 1965, "peak_reserved_mb": 2124, "scene": "synthetic (fastforks bench)", "date": "2026-11-01", "torch": "2.14.1+cu130", "protocol": "median of 5 after 3 warm-up, uint8 CUDA input, original code at the pinned commit, torch.no_grad; peak = first call; float16", "dtype":